{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1281530-talent-tier","id":1281530,"title":"Talent Tier","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-18T10:50:05-08:00","id":1281530,"title":"Talent Tier","content":"Hi guys,<br /> <br /> On TC Core page 74 talents are set as tier 1 (in the Tier table)<br /> On TC Aeon page 125 talents are set as tier 2 (\u201cRemember that ordinary humans are Tier 1 characters, while ordinary psions and Talents are Tier 2 characters.\u201d).<br /> <br /> There are other situations where you can find this, but basically Talwnts are T1 on Core e T2 in Aeon.<br /> <br /> What are your Opinions about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T12:31:12-08:00","id":1281548,"title":"","content":"There were lots of discussions regarding tiers and scale, the most heatly discussed is probably this one: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274835-psions-and-scale\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ions-and-scale</a><br /> <br /> Take one hour off, have some coffee and a snack, sit down, and enjoy the thread/show. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T14:53:27-08:00","id":1281581,"title":"","content":"Ignore the chart on page 74, it just confuses things and is being raised as something to cut from the final book.<br /> <br /> That said Tier != Scale. Tier is much more of an abstract rough estimate of relative power, it doesn\u2019t grant the mechanical benefits of Scale on its own.<br /> <br /> Generally Tier 1 = Baselines<br /> Tier 2 = Talents, Psions, Superiors (&amp; Divergents)<br /> Tier 3 = (Max Mercer?), Proxies, Novas (&amp; Nemeses)<br /> Tier 4 = Terats","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T10:13:28-08:00","id":1281656,"title":"","content":"Some expeculation: Mesmerists and Stalwart are both tier 2 to be in same level of Talents, but if you compare psions powers and mesmerists powers, psions are much more focused but also more powerful (1st level knacks are equivalent to basic powers of most aptitudes).<br /> Do you think they will set Mesmerist as standard Psiads (same level of raw power, but less focused than psions) or do you think they will keep it a little more limited, as happened on Adventure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T10:23:52-08:00","id":1281657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1281530-talent-tier?p=1281656#post1281656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some expeculation: Mesmerists and Stalwart are both tier 2 to be in same level of Talents, but if you compare psions powers and mesmerists powers, psions are much more focused but also more powerful (1st level knacks are equivalent to basic powers of most aptitudes).<br /> Do you think they will set Mesmerist as standard Psiads (same level of raw power, but less focused than psions) or do you think they will keep it a little more limited, as happened on Adventure?</div> </div> </div> </div>My theory is that Mesmerists and Stalwarts will be less powerful than Psions and Superiors in terms of their psychic powers or enhanced atteibutes, but they will round out the difference with Talents in the context of Adventure! by sharing access to Dramatic Editing (as they did in 1E).<br /> <br /> Note that this is an Adventure! specific hypothesis. I\u2019m not suggesting lesser Psychomorphs and Exomorphs running around in the Aberrant or Aeon eras with Dramatic Editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}